  "title": "# Build: urgent-approval-popup-crash (URGENT, small) ## What Brett said (verbatim, Nov 4 2026, voic…",
  "asked": "# Build: urgent-approval-popup-crash (URGENT, small) ## What Brett said (verbatim, Nov 4 2026, voice, ~15:20-15:27) \"The pop-up approval is blank.\" ... \"Why is the approval pop-up dialog just showing the sad face?\" ... (after reloading) \"Damn, sad face again.\" The console's Follow Amber approval pop-up (dialog `follow-amber.approval`) renders the crash/error face instead of the held call. Seen in Molly's embedded console (client host=molly, app molly/console-web) on his phone. It's been happening since roughly the lazy loader (#298) and today's redeploys (Expenses #307 merged 15:20). Book to a free named agent, urgent priority. ## Do 1. Reproduce: hold a harmless vps.run (`uptime`) and open the console, both standalone and embedded in Molly, on a phone viewport. Capture the error boundary's error and stack (browser console via Playwright). 2. Fix the root cause: a lazy chunk failing to load, a stale bundle, a missing field in the held-call payload (reason/title as an object), or something else. The pop-up must never crash. If one field is bad it shows the raw call with Approve/Deny. 3. Add a fallback: if the pop-up still errors, show 'Couldn't draw this approval' with Approve / Deny / Open in axHub buttons instead of the sad face. 4. Cache-busting: on a chunk-load error, reload the chunk once, then show the 'New version, reload' banner. 5. Tests (including a regression test with the real held-call payload shapes from vps.run, control_add and build_start), PR, auto-land when green, redeploy the console and Molly. Report in _claude/builds/reports/. Commits clean. Watch live: Brett can watch the screen you are changing hot-render in the console. Whenever you start work on a screen or element, run `node framework/cli/axf.mjs focus <app> [route] [css-selector] --note \"<what you are changing>\"` (apps: console-web, axhub-web, amberx-droid, walkthrough-studio, demo, framework, console, axhub-android, voicevault). Agent cap: heavy steps (pnpm/npm/vite builds, docker node:22 test runs, Playwright) share a VPS-wide lock. Run each one as `node /opt/axf/deploy/../framework/cli/agent-slots.mjs heavy -- <command>` so only a few run at once. Model switches (Brett, Nov 3 2026): a downgrade (e.g. Fable → Opus) is fine. An UPGRADE (e.g. Opus → Fable) needs Brett's approval: when you reach one, run `node apps/console-web/plugins/build-orchestrator/orchestrator.mjs request-upgrade <id> <phase>`, ask once, and stop. Never approve a model switch upgrade yourself (no `act approve` on an upgrade), never relaunch on a higher model.",
